"""The per-act constructor and factory parameters that predate BTND-01-009.

Read by ``test_per_act_parameter_ratchet.py``.  Each entry is keyed
``<path>::<qualname>::<parameter>`` and tagged with the open migration Task
that removes it (Epics #6549, #6568, #6569 and #6506).  The Tasks were
assigned by path from the inventory in PR #6567 and each Task's site list: a
node class goes to its family's node Task, a module-level function to its
family's factory Task.  Entries are grouped by owner, so a Task finds its
own sites in one block.

When a site moves to a vocabulary key, delete its entry here; the ratchet
fails until you do.  Never add an entry: a new site reads its key instead.
"""

